## 1. Project Setup: Files and Structure `[2:00 – 6:11]`

### 1.1 Creating New Files
The instructor creates a **fresh pair of files** (separate from last session's practice files) to build the real app:
- `main.html` (or `index.html`) — the HTML structure.
- `script.js` — will hold the Vue instance (all the JavaScript logic).

**Why separate files instead of inline `<script>` tags?** As applications grow, keeping HTML and JavaScript logic in separate files is cleaner and more maintainable — a general best practice, not Vue-specific.

### 1.2 Linking Everything Together

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <title>Task Manager</title>
  <script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/vue@2"></script>
</head>
<body>
  <div id="app">
    <!-- All Vue content goes here -->
  </div>

  <script src="./script.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
```

**Line-by-line:**
- `<script src="...vue@2...">` in `<head>` → the **Vue CDN link**, copied over from the previous session's file. This must load first (recall from last session: Vue needs to be available before the browser tries to interpret your Vue-flavored HTML).
- `<div id="app">` → the **root element** where the entire Vue application will mount. Everything the Vue app controls must go inside this div.
- `<script src="./script.js">` → links your own application logic file. The `./` means "look in the same directory (root folder) as this HTML file."

> ⚠️ **Common Mistake:** Forgetting to link `script.js` at all, or linking it *before* the Vue CDN script — this breaks everything because your code would try to use `Vue` before it's defined.

### 1.3 Creating the Vue Instance

```javascript
const app = new Vue({
  el: '#app',
  data: {
    // data properties will go here
  }
});
```

- `const app` → note the instructor now uses `const` (a variable that cannot be reassigned) instead of `var`, since we don't intend to reassign `app` to something else later. This is a minor stylistic upgrade from before.
- `new Vue({...})` → same pattern as last session: creates a new Vue instance.
- `el: '#app'` → mounts to the div with `id="app"`.
- `data: {...}` → will hold all our task-related state (covered next).

### ✅ Section 1 Summary
- Two files: `main.html` (structure) + `script.js` (logic), linked via `<script src>`.
- One Vue app = one root div (`#app`) = one `new Vue({...})` instance.
- `const` used here since the app variable itself won't be reassigned.

