## 9. Conditionally Hiding the "Mark Complete" Button Once Done `[1:26:44 – 1:28:39]`

### The Refinement
Once a task is marked complete, showing a "Mark as Complete" button next to it no longer makes sense. Let's hide it.

```html
<td>
  <button v-if="!task.isCompleted" @click="markComplete(task.id)">
    Mark as Complete
  </button>
  <span v-else>✓ Completed</span>
</td>
```

- Same pattern as Section 7: `v-if="!task.isCompleted"` shows the button only while the task is still pending; `v-else` shows a simple confirmation text (or you could show nothing at all, or a "Completed" label) once done.

> 💡 **Design principle demonstrated here:** UI elements (not just text, but entire interactive controls like buttons) can be conditionally rendered based on data state — this is a very common real-world pattern (e.g., hiding a "Submit" button after form submission, hiding a "Follow" button after you've already followed someone).

### ✅ Section 9 Summary
- `v-if`/`v-else` isn't limited to text — you can conditionally show/hide entire interactive elements like buttons.

